WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.169
Was shocked by

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:03.803
the degree of

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.305
sensitivity in these documents

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.407
and how many there were, frankly.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.010
And so the government's agenda

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.812
was to get those protect those documents

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.613
and get them out.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.515
And I think it was perfectly appropriate

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.249
to do that.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.351
It was the right thing to do.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.352
And I think the counts

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.254
under the Espionage Act

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.089
that he willfully retained

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.592
those documents are solid counts.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:27.827
That, of course, was former

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:28.862
Attorney General Bill Barr

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.796
saying he's shocked

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.231
by how sensitive the documents

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.999
are at the center of the new indictment

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.734
against his old boss, his old boss,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.870
who defended quite often in the past.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.105
I want to read a specific paragraph

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.206
from that indictment

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.375
that gets what Barr was talking about.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.676
And it says, quote,

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.844
The Justice Department alleges

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.578
the documents

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.247
included information

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.481
regarding defense

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:48.982
and weapons

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:49.916
capabilities of both

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.885
the United States and foreign countries,

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.219
our nuclear programs,

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.487
potential vulnerabilities

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.488
of the United States

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.524
and its allies to military attack

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.358
and plans

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.859
for possible retaliation

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.195
in response to foreign attack.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.930
Now, it goes on to say, the unauthorized

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.932
disclosure of these classified documents

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.901
could put at risk the national security

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.169
of the United States

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.003
foreign relations

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.671
and the safety of the United States

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.307
military and human sources.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.475
I want to bring in Donald Trump's

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.976
former national security adviser,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.478
John Bolton. He joins us now.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.612
He also served as the U.S.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.281
ambassador to the United Nations.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.382
And Ambassador Bolton,

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.484
look, you are neither secretive

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.185
nor subtle

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.019
about your desire

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.320
to see the former president

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.955
out of the race.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.658
For president or to be a candidate

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:32.792
for president anymore.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.327
And we want to ask about the politics,

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.096
because I want to ask you about what

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.897
these documents actually mean.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.998
There's a lot of classification

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:39.632
and markings.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.800
There's a lot of

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.202
words and descriptions

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.337
that people might not understand.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.105
Tell people

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.639
from a national security perspective

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.408
what's in the documents

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.409
laid out in this indictment.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.612
Well, of course,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.113
neither I

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.347
nor anybody else

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.482
not involved in the case

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.717
knows what's in the documents yet.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.652
But I do know what kinds of documents

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.554
were put in front of the president

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.455
during my time,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:02.789
I'm sure,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.225
during the entire four years of his term.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.228
And they did go to absolute

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.596
the most important secrets

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.131
that the United States

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.465
has, directly

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.367
affecting national security, directly

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.802
affecting the lives, lives

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.737
and safety of our service members

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.472
and our civilian population.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.840
If he has anything

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.509
like what the complaint

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.843
what the indictment alleges,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.744
and of course, the government

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.279
will have to prove it

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.780
then, that he has committed

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.716
very serious crimes.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.218
This is this is a devastating indictment.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.520
I speak here as an alumnus

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.688
of the Justice Department myself,

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:36.656
because not only is

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.592
it powerful, it's very narrowly tailored.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:40.126
They didn't

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.728
throw everything up against the wall

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.096
to see what would stick.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.098
This really is a rifle shot.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.533
And I think it's

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.835
it should be the end of Donald Trump's

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.236
political career.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.304
He's obviously made clear

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:51.871
he doesn't think

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.640
that's going to be the case.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.941
It should be no surprise to anybody.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:55.775
But I do want to ask you,

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.643
still on the documents,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.143
I know you don't know

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.478
the specific documents themselves,

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.078
but when you look

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.080
at the classification levels.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.881
Can you explain to people

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.082
how difficult it would be

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.151
for an average government

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:05.785
employee, one,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.120
to have access to them in the first place

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.522
and to to be able to get them out of

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.592
compartmentalized area

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.126
where you're supposed

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.995
to be reading secretive documents

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.631
Well, it will vary depending

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.033
on the level of the employee

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.700
and where they are.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.701
My office,

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.236
my old office at the White House,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.338
the whole office was a skiff

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.273
because we just were drowning

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.209
in classified information.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.310
And at least in theory,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.144
the Oval Office

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.746
ought to be a pretty safe place, too.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.448
And it's very important, obviously,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.583
to give the president

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.384
all the information

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:38.851
he needs

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.553
to make a decision, unfortunately.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.288
Trump didn't pay too much attention

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.923
to a lot of what he was given,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.558
but he paid enough attention to it

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.594
to have a constant fixation

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.162
of trying to hold on to documents.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.164
A lot of things we got back from him.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.433
Obviously, a lot of things we didn't.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.268
I've been

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:55.835
interested to

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.304
see some of your Republican counterparts

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:01.140
maybe aren't as hyperbolic,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.975
I guess would be the word

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.343
on some things related to the former

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.612
president saying, look, this isn't great,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.213
but a trial

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.982
or an indictment of a former president

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:09.582
and the

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.083
the frontrunner

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:10.583
in the Republican

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.219
nomination is far worse for the country

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.854
than what actually happened here.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:18.391
How do you what do you make of that?

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.727
Well, I don't buy that argument at all.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.928
But but look, give

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:22.662
give those

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.396
who are saying it's

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.065
some credit, assume, for example,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.267
for the sake of discussion

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.935
that Hillary Clinton Joe Biden, Hunter

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.870
Biden, fill in the blank,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.138
should should be indicted,

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.273
should be prosecuted.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.140
And the failure

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.609
to do so constitutes a double standard.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.144
Just assume that for purposes

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.212
of discussion.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.046
Now, look at this

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.048
indictment of Donald Trump.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.484
Do those people who make that complaint

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:45.752
say, therefore,

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.487
the answer is not to prosecute

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.187
Donald Trump,

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.890
that the response to a double standard

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.326
is to move to no standard at all?

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.327
Absolutely not.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.296
You know, Republicans used to believe

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.197
that not prosecuting criminals

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.299
led to more crime.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.200
The answer here is take the politics

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.502
out of the decision

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.603
and in this case,

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.538
proceed with the prosecution

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.206
and do the same for anybody else

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.176
who does anything even remotely like it.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.612
So then why is every single other top

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.947
Republican candidate seemingly

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.049
critical of the indictment

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.885
and seemingly afraid to attack him on it?

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.655
I don't know, honestly.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.289
You know,

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.023
we hear a lot

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.125
these days about public opinion polls

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.093
taken over the weekend.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.428
Political leadership

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.529
doesn't take

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.697
a public opinion

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.231
polls as blocks of granite.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:32.865
They're interesting

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.000
pieces of information.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.169
Political leaders change public opinion.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.271
I think it's critical

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.439
for those who seek to be

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.606
the Republican nominee

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.175
to tell Republican voters

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.843
the truth about this indictment.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.813
I wish the RNC could email

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.181
a copy of the indictment

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.182
to every registered

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.350
Republican in the country.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.217
And I'd simply say

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.752
I'm not going to make a lot of arguments

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:53.252
with them.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.021
Just read the indictment

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:55.922
and ask yourself

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.357
if the government can prove

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.791
what they allege here.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:02.095
Shouldn't this man go to jail?

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:03.663
One of the things that I've been

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.530
trying to get my head around

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.933
in terms of the scale of

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.801
what happened here or what's alleged

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.136
here is the why

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.537
Why would the president take it?

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:11.637
You know,

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:12.872
there's a lot of theories out there

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.874
as to why he would want these documents.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:15.608
You were with him.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.809
You saw him in action

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.044
at a very close level.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:18.811
Why do you think

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.712
what was the intent here?

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.183
Well, I'm not sure I can give

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:24.817
you a good answer,

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.018
but I would say this

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.087
throughout my 17 months there.

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.123
It's perfectly clear

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.691
that Donald Trump addressed

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:34.160
almost everything that came before him

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.429
through the prism of the question,

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:39.132
how does this benefit Donald Trump?

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:41.367
And so I think a lot of these documents

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.935
he may have just thought were cool,

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:43.469
a lot of it

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:44.771
he thought might be souvenirs,

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:45.872
a lot of me thought

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.240
might be useful to him later.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.808
I can't answer the question

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.510
until I see the document.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:50.977
But,

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:52.445
well,

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:53.546
there are a lot of theories

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:54.914
that he could use it

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.049
as information against his enemies,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.050
that he could

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:00.186
give it to people in exchange for favors.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:01.287
We don't know.

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:01.921
And frankly,

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.090
I don't think speculating about

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.858
the reasons is all that helpful.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.160
The simple fact

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.562
he had the documents for any reason

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.164
or no reason

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:13.032
should subject him to prosecution

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:16.502
How do you think this ends

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.171
for the former president

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.340
Well, I think if I were

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.341
an innocent person,

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.409
if I were Donald Trump

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:24.177
and I were innocent,

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:24.811
I'd be saying

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:27.313
I want this insult to my integrity.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.415
I use these words loosely removed

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.750
as soon as possible.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.618
I'm prepared to waive a lot of frivolous

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:33.686
procedural motions.

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:34.987
I want to go to trial

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.789
in the next 60 days.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.357
I don't want to drag this out.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.959
I'm innocent. I can prove it.

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.327
Let's go.

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.229
Does anybody think Donald Trump's

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:44.163
really going to do that?

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.466
I hope the Justice Department

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.601
really does try for a speedy trial

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:50.102
because frankly, the sooner

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.904
it goes to a jury

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.840
and we find out their answer, whatever,

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.441
whatever that answer is going to be,

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.709
the better for the country.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.177
Justice delayed, as they say,

00:07:58.177 --> 00:07:59.245
is justice denied.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:00.213
And the court

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.848
should not let Donald

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:04.050
Trump get the kind of delay I suspect

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.951
he wants.

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:06.452
Ambassador John Bolton, thanks so much

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:06.919
for your time, sir.

